{"path":"numeric/complex/imaginary","title":"imaginary","titleHtml":"imaginary","originalUrl":"https://en.cppreference.com/w/c/numeric/complex/imaginary","section":"numeric","kind":"page","summary":"This macro expands to the keyword _Imaginary.","html":"<table class=\"t-dcl-begin\"><tbody>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc-header\">\n<td> <div>Defined in header <code><a href=\"/w/c/numeric/complex\"><code>&lt;complex.h&gt;</code></a></code>\n </div></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl t-since-c99\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi c source-c\"><span class=\"co2\">#define imaginary _Imaginary</span></span></div></td>\n<td class=\"t-dcl-nopad\">  </td>\n<td> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-c99\">(since C99)</span> </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl-sep\"><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p>This macro expands to the keyword <a href=\"/w/c/keyword/_Imaginary\"><code>_Imaginary</code></a>.\n</p><p>This is a convenience macro that makes it possible to use <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi c source-c\"><span class=\"kw4\">float</span> imaginary</span></code>, <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi c source-c\"><span class=\"kw4\">double</span> imaginary</span></code>, and <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi c source-c\"><span class=\"kw4\">long</span> <span class=\"kw4\">double</span> imaginary</span></code> as an alternative way to write the three pure imaginary C types <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi c source-c\"><span class=\"kw4\">float</span> _Imaginary</span></code>, <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi c source-c\"><span class=\"kw4\">double</span> _Imaginary</span></code>, and <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi c source-c\"><span class=\"kw4\">long</span> <span class=\"kw4\">double</span> _Imaginary</span></code>\n</p><p>As with any pure imaginary number support in C, this macro is only defined if the imaginary numbers are supported.\n</p>\n<table class=\"t-rev-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-rev t-since-c99 t-until-c11\"><td>\n<p>A compiler that defines <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi c source-c\">__STDC_IEC_559_COMPLEX__</span></code> is not required to support imaginary numbers. POSIX recommends checking if the macro <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi c source-c\"><a href=\"/w/c/numeric/complex/Imaginary_I\"><span class=\"kw745\">_Imaginary_I</span></a></span></code> is defined to identify imaginary number support.\n</p>\n</td>\n<td><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-c99\">(since C99)</span><br><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-until-c11\">(until C11)</span></td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-rev t-since-c11\"><td>\n<p>Imaginary numbers are supported if <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi c source-c\">__STDC_IEC_559_COMPLEX__</span></code> is defined.\n</p>\n</td>\n<td><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-c11\">(since C11)</span></td></tr>\n</table>\n<h3 id=\"Notes\">Notes</h3>\n<p>Programs are allowed to undefine and perhaps redefine the <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi c source-c\">imaginary</span></code> macro.\n</p><p>To date, only Oracle C compiler is known to have implemented imaginary types.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Example\">Example</h3>\n<div class=\"t-example\">\n<pre data-lang=\"c\"><code><span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;stdio.h&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;complex.h&gt;</span>\n&nbsp;\n<span class=\"kw4\">int</span> main<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"kw4\">void</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">{</span>\n    <span class=\"kw4\">double</span> imaginary i <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> <span class=\"sy2\">-</span><span class=\"nu16\">2.0</span><span class=\"sy2\">*</span>I<span class=\"sy4\">;</span> <span class=\"co1\">// pure imaginary</span>\n    <span class=\"kw4\">double</span> f <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> <span class=\"nu16\">1.0</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span> <span class=\"co1\">// pure real</span>\n    <span class=\"kw4\">double</span> <a href=\"/w/c/numeric/complex/complex\"><span class=\"kw743\">complex</span></a> z <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> f <span class=\"sy2\">+</span> i<span class=\"sy4\">;</span> <span class=\"co1\">// complex number</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/c/io/fprintf\"><span class=\"kw850\">printf</span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"st0\">\"z =&nbsp;%.1f%+.1fi<span class=\"es1\">\\n</span>\"</span>, <a href=\"/w/c/numeric/complex/creal\"><span class=\"kw753\">creal</span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span>z<span class=\"br0\">)</span>, <a href=\"/w/c/numeric/complex/cimag\"><span class=\"kw750\">cimag</span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span>z<span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">}</span></code></pre>\n<p>Output:\n</p>\n<pre data-output=\"1\"><code>z = 1.0-2.0i</code></pre> \n</div>\n<h3 id=\"References\">References</h3>\n<div class=\"t-ref-std-17\">\n<ul><li> C17 standard (ISO/IEC 9899:2018): \n</li></ul>\n<dl><dd><ul><li> 7.3.1/5 imaginary (p: 136)\n</li></ul>\n</dd></dl>\n<dl><dd><ul><li> G.6/1 imaginary (p: 391-392)\n</li></ul>\n</dd></dl>\n</div>\n<div class=\"t-ref-std-11\">\n<ul><li> C11 standard (ISO/IEC 9899:2011): \n</li></ul>\n<dl><dd><ul><li> 7.3.1/5 imaginary (p: 188)\n</li></ul>\n</dd></dl>\n<dl><dd><ul><li> G.6/1 imaginary (p: 537)\n</li></ul>\n</dd></dl>\n</div>\n<div class=\"t-ref-std-c99\">\n<ul><li> C99 standard (ISO/IEC 9899:1999): \n</li></ul>\n<dl><dd><ul><li> 7.3.1/3 imaginary (p: 170)\n</li></ul>\n</dd></dl>\n<dl><dd><ul><li> G.6/1 imaginary (p: 472)\n</li></ul>\n</dd></dl>\n</div>\n<h3 id=\"See_also\">See also</h3>\n<table class=\"t-dsc-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/c/numeric/complex/complex\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>complex</span></span></a></div><div><span class=\"t-lines\"><span><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-c99\">(C99)</span></span></span></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>   complex type macro  <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(keyword macro)</span> </td></tr>\n</table>","headings":[{"depth":3,"text":"Notes","id":"Notes"},{"depth":3,"text":"Example","id":"Example"},{"depth":3,"text":"References","id":"References"},{"depth":3,"text":"See also","id":"See_also"}],"breadcrumbs":[{"path":"","title":"C reference"},{"path":"numeric","title":"Numerics"},{"path":"numeric/complex","title":"Complex number arithmetic"}],"children":[],"map":{"label":"imaginary","children":[{"label":"Declarations","note":"1 declaration. This macro expands to the keyword _Imaginary."},{"label":"Notes","note":"Programs are allowed to undefine and perhaps redefine the imaginary macro."},{"label":"Example"},{"label":"See also","children":[{"label":"complex","note":"complex type macro"}]}]},"standards":["C99","C11"],"wordCount":227,"codeBlockCount":2}
